0 -14 Td (---) Tj
0 -14 Td (## 1. Client Objective \(As Understood\)) Tj
0 -14 Td (You are considering purchasing 85 acres of rural land at Murrundi Creek Road, Yarran for $480,000. Your stated objectives are:) Tj
0 -14 Td (1. Build a weekend retreat / holiday home) Tj
0 -14 Td (2. Potential future subdivision \(2-3 lots\)) Tj
0 -14 Td (3. Passive income from grazing lease) Tj
0 -14 Td (4. Long-term family asset \(generational wealth\)) Tj
0 -14 Td (Your risk tolerance is moderate, with emphasis on a clear pathway to development.) Tj
0 -14 Td (---) Tj
0 -14 Td (## 2. Information Snapshot) Tj
0 -14 Td (### Known Facts) Tj
0 -14 Td (- Property is 85 acres, zoned RU1 Primary Production) Tj
0 -14 Td (- Freehold title, no caveats) Tj
0 -14 Td (- Dwelling is permitted under zoning \(subject to approvals\)) Tj
0 -14 Td (- AHIMS search identifies **3 registered Aboriginal heritage sites** on the property) Tj
0 -14 Td (- Site types include: scarred tree, artifact scatter, **potential burial site**) Tj
0 -14 Td (- Active **native title claim** \(Yarran Peoples\) covers this area) Tj
0 -14 Td (- No Indigenous Land Use Agreement exists) Tj
0 -14 Td (### Key Constraints) Tj
0 -14 Td (- Heritage sites protected under NSW National Parks and Wildlife Act 1974) Tj
0 -14 Td (- Disturbing Aboriginal objects: penalties up to $1.1 million and/or imprisonment) Tj
0 -14 Td (- Any ground disturbance requires Aboriginal Heritage Impact Permit \(AHIP\)) Tj
0 -14 Td (- AHIP process: 12-24 months, outcome uncertain) Tj
0 -14 Td (- Native title determination: typically 5-10 years) Tj
0 -14 Td (---) Tj
0 -14 Td (## 3. TRUE Assessment Summary) Tj
0 -14 Td (Heritage constraints are definitively established through AHIMS and NNTT searches. Three registered sites and an active native title claim create clear, verifiable barriers to development.) Tj
0 -14 Td (**TRUE Status: PASS \(constraints are known and bounded\)**) Tj
0 -14 Td (---) Tj
0 -14 Td (## 4. NORTH Assessment Summary) Tj
0 -14 Td (The regulatory pathway to development is 5-12+ years with uncertain outcome. Heritage protection is strengthening, not weakening. Client's 90-day settlement and development objectives are incompatible with the actual regulatory timeline.) Tj
0 -14 Td (**NORTH Status: FAIL ? Decision does not make sense over time**) Tj
0 -14 Td (---) Tj
0 -14 Td (## 5. ALIGNED Assessment Summary) Tj
0 -14 Td (Client objectives \(dwelling, subdivision, development-based wealth\) are fundamentally misaligned with property constraints. The property may suit a buyer seeking undeveloped rural land, but it does not suit these clients' stated objectives.) Tj
0 -14 Td (**ALIGNED Status: FAIL ? Objectives misaligned with constraints**) Tj
0 -14 Td (---) Tj
0 -14 Td (## 6. Decision State) Tj
0 -14 Td (- [ ] Proceed) Tj
0 -14 Td (- [ ] Pause) Tj
0 -14 Td (- [x] Avoid / Walk Away) Tj
0 -14 Td (---) Tj
0 -14 Td (## 7. Rationale Summary) Tj
0 -14 Td (This property is not suitable for your stated objectives. The key reasons are:) Tj
0 -14 Td (1. **Heritage sites prevent practical development.** Three registered Aboriginal heritage sites, including a potential burial site, create severe constraints on any ground disturbance. The AHIP process takes 12-24 months with uncertain outcome, and approval is less likely given the presence of a potential burial site.) Tj
0 -14 Td (2. **Native title claim adds further uncertainty.** The active native title claim will take 5-10 years to determine. Development and subdivision may require negotiation with or consent from native title holders, whose rights are not yet defined.) Tj
0 -14 Td (3. **Your timeline is incompatible with reality.** A 90-day settlement assumes you can proceed with development planning. In practice, you would be purchasing land where development rights are uncertain for 5+ years.) Tj
0 -14 Td (4. **Your objectives require development that may never be approved.** Building a dwelling and subdividing are your primary goals. This property cannot deliver those goals within any reasonable timeframe.) Tj
ET
